#
#   Test build adjustments to the development configuration.
#
#   The development configuration itself lives in sdkconfig.develop in the root of the
#   repository and is shared with the application.  Nothing is copied here: this file
#   holds only the settings that have to differ because the tests are built from a
#   project directory of their own, and it is merged after the shared file so that what
#   it says wins.
#
#   ESP-IDF resolves the partition table file against the project directory, which is
#   this directory rather than the root of the repository, so the name the shared file
#   gives it does not find the file from here.  This points it back at the one file in
#   the root, so that the tests and the application are built against the same partition
#   table rather than against two copies that can drift apart.
#
CONFIG_PARTITION_TABLE_CUSTOM_FILENAME="../partitions-develop.csv"
CONFIG_PARTITION_TABLE_FILENAME="../partitions-develop.csv"

#
#   The development configuration aborts on any failed allocation, which stops a
#   diagnostic build at the allocation that ran out.  The tests need the release
#   behaviour instead, where the allocator returns nullptr, so the code handling running
#   out of memory can be tested at all (issue #162).  A test that runs out of memory by
#   accident now fails where the nullptr is used rather than at the allocation.
#
# CONFIG_HEAP_ABORT_WHEN_ALLOCATION_FAILS is not set
